### Test 6 — Sesión en otro dispositivo tras cerrar sesión en todos lados (logout-all)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:57011/api/v1
@email = qa-test6-{{$timestamp}}@example.com
@password = QaPassword123!

### 6.1 Dispositivo A se registra y activa plan dolly
# @name deviceA
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "fullName": "QA Multi Device"
}

@accessA = {{deviceA.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}}
@refreshA = {{deviceA.response.body.data.tokens.refreshToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/user/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{accessA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tier": "dolly"
}

### 6.2 Dispositivo B inicia sesión independiente
# @name deviceB
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@accessB = {{deviceB.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}}
@refreshB = {{deviceB.response.body.data.tokens.refreshToken}}

### 6.3 Ambos dispositivos acceden antes de logout-all -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessB}}

### 6.4 Dispositivo A ejecuta logout-all -> 200 OK (revoca todos los refresh tokens)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{accessA}}

### 6.5 Dispositivo B aún puede operar brevemente mientras su access token corto no haya expirado -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessB}}

### 6.6 Pero Dispositivo B ya NO puede refrescar la sesión -> 401 AUTH_TOKEN_INVALID
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshB}}"
}

### Tampoco Dispositivo A puede refrescar su refresh token previo -> 401 AUTH_TOKEN_INVALID
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshA}}"
}
